# E §11 (tally 2.1.3, issue #58): `REQ-ASK` prints `no ask <q>`, "q the first such ask in the request's order", and
# "the request is refused": the request names q (an ask of the reality), then zz and yy (neither is). zz is the first
# unknown in the request's order (yy would be first by code point), and q isn't answered: the run prints the one
# refusal. Was `refused: LOAD-NAME no ask zz`.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input y: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  y = 1

ask q: y
=== expect q zz yy
refused: REQ-ASK no ask zz
